      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name}: The intent of this thread was for accessibility, did not regard my neighboring post.\nTo clarify what my suggestion entailed:\nThe current process is...\n(Already be laying down with a horizon position set.)\n1. Reset horizon orientation\n2. Stand up and calibrate FBT\n3. Reset the horizon adjustment to what you had before\nI had thought of the idea of that this process could save your horizon position during the calibration process, so that it would not be necessary to reset and then re-adjust it, instead it would do that automatically when you press the \"Calibrate FBT\" option.\nThe process requires a reset to the horizon to properly calibrate. If you do not reset the horizon when calibrating, it will not be synchronized with the avatar.\nOr maybe instead have the \"Calibrate FBT\" button to double as a horizon reset button, since you have to stand up to calibrate anyway.\nI hope that this makes sense.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
